1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Hi everyone, I'm Etta, product manager
for MONA.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,800
This video is an apology.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:13,000
On the 15th, at the L05 launch,

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,400
I saw a lot of videos about myself

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:22,000
and a lot of comments pointing things out.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,900
Some of you were uncomfortable with
"lao deng",

7
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:31,000
some questioned my professionalism,

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
and some attacked how I look and my age.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,200
And because of the way I spoke,

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:42,500
some of you were left feeling bad about
the L05.

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,500
That is on me.

12
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,400
So I want to say a proper sorry to all
of you.

13
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,400
I would still like to explain.

14
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,100
The word "lao deng" -

15
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,100
it is something we use as a joke among
ourselves all the time.

16
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:04,100
We tease Guang-ge and the old hands
with it.

17
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:07,600
Nobody thought anything of it -

18
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,600
we just took it as a joke.

19
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:16,100
But I never realised that in public
it makes people uncomfortable.

20
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:21,600
To me it was a joke; to people who don't
know us,

21
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,600
it sounds like something else entirely.

22
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,600
So I am very sorry for the discomfort.

23
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:32,600
It was also my first time on a stage
that big,

24
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:37,600
and I wanted to share the stories behind
the product -

25
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:42,100
so some of our in-jokes went up there
with me.

26
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:45,100
That was me not thinking it through.

27
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:49,600
And what we were mocking was never age.

28
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,600
What we meant to criticise

29
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,600
is the same thinking and the same stock
language for every car.

30
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,600
That fixed mindset was the target.

31
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:01,600
Of course, everyone's choice is their own;

32
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:05,600
I still should not have used that word
to say it.

33
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:08,600
I will be much more careful from now on.

34
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:12,600
On 29 October the L05 goes on sale.

35
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:18,600
Our product and marketing teams are doing
the final work,

36
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:24,600
and I hope we explain the car better then.

37
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:28,600
Please keep an eye on it,

38
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,600
because we put a great deal into it -

39
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,600
it really is a good car.

40
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:39,600
So please do not let the discussion about
my remarks

41
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:46,600
change how you feel about the L05.

42
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,600
I really hope you like it.

43
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,600
Once again, I'm sorry,

44
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:55,600
and thank you for the suggestions.

45
00:02:55,600 --> 00:03:00,600
I'll manage the way I speak much better.

46
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:06,600
If you have questions about the L05,

47
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,600
or about things we could have done better,

48
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,600
ask me - my colleagues and I will answer
what we can.

49
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:18,600
Again, sorry, and thank you.

50
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:24,600
I hope you can accept my apology.

51
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,900
Thank you.
